The orbit theme's faces (~/.config/themes/orbit/).

All three families come from Google Fonts' repository, which carries each
upstream project's released TTFs together with its licence:
    https://github.com/google/fonts   (branch main)
All are under the SIL Open Font License 1.1 (OFL-1.1): free to use, bundle
and redistribute, not to sell on their own; the licence text travels with
the files (OFL-Barlow.txt, OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt here). No file was
modified.

Barlow -- the UI face (theme.conf font=): the bar, the toolbox, the popup
    panels, the launcher, mako, mpv's OSD and subtitles, Nautilus's document
    face.
    By Jeremy Tribby (The Barlow Project, https://github.com/jpt/barlow),
    version 1.408. A slightly rounded, low-contrast grotesk drawn after
    California's highway signs and licence plates -- the plain, engineered
    sans of a console label or a placard on a rack, which is the look the
    theme is after (a mission-control console), while staying soft enough
    to read for hours. Static weights, so every weight the stylesheets ask
    for is a real cut: Regular, Medium (the panels' 500), SemiBold (the
    bar's 600), Bold, and Italic.
    Figures: proportional by default, with a tabular "tnum" feature -- the
    base stylesheets ask for tnum on every rule, so the bar's readouts and
    the panels' numbers do not twitch.
    Metrics: 1000 units per em, a 1.20 em line (IBM Plex Sans: 1.30), and
    narrower letters than Plex -- so most panels come out a little smaller
    than cyberpunk's (~/.config/themes/orbit/panel.css's header has the
    measured sizes).
    Files:  Barlow-Regular.ttf  Barlow-Medium.ttf  Barlow-SemiBold.ttf
            Barlow-Bold.ttf     Barlow-Italic.ttf
    Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/barlow/<file>
            licence: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/barlow/OFL.txt
                     (saved as OFL-Barlow.txt)

Barlow Semi Condensed -- the label face: headings and section labels in the
    panels (.kb-heading, the month, the shortcuts title), the bar's date,
    the LLM chat's headings. Set by name in the stylesheets, not by font=.
    The same design (same project, same version 1.408) at a narrower width,
    so small letter-spaced labels stay compact -- the console's engraved
    legend under a readout.
    Files:  BarlowSemiCondensed-Regular.ttf  BarlowSemiCondensed-Medium.ttf
            BarlowSemiCondensed-SemiBold.ttf BarlowSemiCondensed-Bold.ttf
    Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/barlowsemicondensed/<file>
            licence: the same OFL text as Barlow's (same copyright line),
            https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/barlowsemicondensed/OFL.txt

    Coverage of both Barlow families: 525 code points -- Latin, Latin-1,
    Latin Extended-A/B and Vietnamese (Latin Extended Additional); four
    Greek letters only; no Cyrillic; no arrows (U+2190..), no U+25B8 "▸",
    no "✓". fontconfig falls back per glyph to IBM Plex Sans (theme.conf
    font= lists it second; Plex has the arrows and ✓, but not ▸), and Font
    Awesome is the icon fallback as everywhere. So a "▸" prompt is best
    set in JetBrains Mono, which has it.

JetBrains Mono -- the readout and terminal face (term.font=, font_mono=):
    the bar's clock and workspace keys, the shortcuts panel's key caps,
    COSMIC Terminal, kitty, mpv's console, code in the LLM chat, Nautilus's
    monospace.
    By JetBrains (Philipp Nurullin, Konstantin Bulenkov;
    https://github.com/JetBrains/JetBrainsMono), version 2.211. A coding
    face with a tall x-height, plain unambiguous shapes (0/O, 1/l/I) and
    every glyph one cell (600/1000 em) wide -- a clock or a counter in it
    can never change width. Variable: one wght axis, 100-800, so the 500 /
    600 the stylesheets ask for are exact; the Italic is its own variable
    file. COSMIC Terminal needs a Bold, which the axis provides (theme.py
    check confirms it).
    Coverage: 976 code points -- Latin, Latin Extended, Greek, Cyrillic,
    arrows, box drawing, ▸.
    Files:  JetBrainsMono[wght].ttf  JetBrainsMono-Italic[wght].ttf
    Source: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/jetbrainsmono/JetBrainsMono%5Bwght%5D.ttf
            https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/jetbrainsmono/JetBrainsMono-Italic%5Bwght%5D.ttf
            licence: https://raw.githubusercontent.com/google/fonts/main/ofl/jetbrainsmono/OFL.txt
                     (saved as OFL-JetBrainsMono.txt)

Installed by copying into this folder and
    fc-cache -f ~/.local/share/fonts
then checked with `fc-list | grep themes/orbit`: families Barlow, Barlow
Semi Condensed and JetBrains Mono, every style listed above.
If any is missing: download the files again from the URLs above (or
`sudo dnf install jetbrains-mono-fonts` for the mono: Fedora's package of
the same face, 2.304 in fc44 -- a later release than the 2.211 here) and
rerun fc-cache.

Fetched 2026-10-24 (main branch; versions as read from each file's name
table: Barlow 1.408, JetBrains Mono 2.211).

